WEBVTT

1
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:29.401
Kelly Costello. Now, just let us, we'll carefully introduce ourselves.

2
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:34.800
In the room here we have the officials from MB,

3
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.590
and they will be listening to this, and then we'll be speaking to them afterwards.

4
00:00:40.981 --> 00:00:43.800
I'm Greg O'Connor. I'm the chair of the Select Committee.

5
00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:45.901
I'm seated at the center of the table.

6
00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:47.520
On my left is-

7
00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:53.160
Kia ora. I'm Cindy Wade-Brown. Nice to see you on the Zoom

8
00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:55.321
And on my right-

9
00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.580
Kia ora koutou. I'm Brett Young, Member of Parliament for Maungakiekie

10
00:01:00.301 --> 00:01:04.981
And I'm Andrew Bayly, Auckland Central member

11
00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:10.470
All right. Now, Ms. Kelly Costello, do you mind if I-- Aine is it?

12
00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:11.821
Aine, yep.

13
00:01:11.865 --> 00:01:16.321
Aine. If you don't mind if, Aine. If you're happy with me calling Aine?

14
00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:16.620
Yeah

15
00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:21.720
And if you're happy. So we've got your submission, and we've read it.

16
00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:26.461
If you've got 10 minutes to use how you will, feel free to speak to it.

17
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.510
But it would be useful if you left some time for questions at the end for the

18
00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:31.470
members. So,

19
00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:33.180
introduce yourself.

20
00:01:33.211 --> 00:01:36.750
Thank you. We were indicated that we had 15 minutes in total.

21
00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:37.740
Is that still the case?

22
00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:39.211
Yes.

23
00:01:39.271 --> 00:01:41.654
Oh, my apologies. You do have 15 minutes, yes.

24
00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.141
There we go. There we go.

25
00:01:43.305 --> 00:01:46.290
Thank you. So yeah, we will do that.

26
00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:50.745
So here with me is Nithin Mankil and Frans Merrits.

27
00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:57.120
But tena koutou, thank you all for your time today and for introducing yourselves.

28
00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:04.035
So my name is Aine, and Nithin and Frans are here from Migrants

29
00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.705
Against the Acceptable Standard of Health Aotearoa, MASHAA.

30
00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:12.300
And as immigrants to Aotearoa, we've seen the beautiful and welcoming side of this

31
00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:17.700
country, but we also continue to feel the impact of a policy that has the opposite

32
00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:22.351
effect by deeming many migrants with disabilities and health conditions cost

33
00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:23.400
burdens to the state.

34
00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:30.000
MASHAA does two linked things. We systemically advocate to abolish the acceptable

35
00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:34.020
standard of health requirements, and we support those impacted now.

36
00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:39.900
So now I'd like to hand to Nithin and then to Frans, who will both share what

37
00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:44.400
impact the ASSH requirements have had on them and on their families' lives.

38
00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:46.141
So over to you, Nithin.

39
00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:47.910
Well, welcome, gentlemen.

40
00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:50.010
Thank you for the time.

41
00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:56.010
My name is Nithin Mankil, and I am the father of Aiden Nithin, a six-year-old boy.

42
00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.290
I'm writing on behalf of my family.

43
00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:03.540
My wife and I are both holders of New Zealand residence visa.

44
00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:08.730
We are originally from Kerala, India and are currently living in Nelson.

45
00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:14.701
We both are health professional, myself registered nurse, and my wife is a

46
00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.755
healthcare assistant. We initially submitted a family residence visa application

47
00:03:20.041 --> 00:03:24.480
that include our son, Aiden, who was on general visitor visa at that time.

48
00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:30.120
During the medical examination in New Zealand, Aiden was diagnosed with autism

49
00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:35.940
spectrum disorder. Following this, immigration officer advised us over the phone to

50
00:03:35.969 --> 00:03:41.760
remove Aiden from the residency application and proceed without him, to apply for a

51
00:03:41.791 --> 00:03:43.590
different visa category for

52
00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:50.310
him separately, as he didn't meet the acceptable standard of health requirement.

53
00:03:50.851 --> 00:03:54.976
Based on that advice, we continue our application, and my wife and I granted a

54
00:03:55.171 --> 00:04:01.050
residency visa in June 2025. As Aiden's visitor visa was nearly expired,

55
00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.796
I submitted a new visa application.

56
00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:08.250
Unfortunately, this application was declined, as a result, Aiden become unlawful.

57
00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:14.370
We then appealed for Honorable Associate Minister Immigration, Chris Penk, on

58
00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:20.550
fourth August 2025. On November 2025, we received

59
00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:23.970
a response stating that the minister can't able to intervene in this matter.

60
00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:30.420
This situation was extremely distressing and heartbreaking for our family.

61
00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:35.130
The thought of being separated from our only child is emotionally overwhelming.

62
00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:40.230
We are mentally exhausted, often in tears all the days, and struggling to find a

63
00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:44.490
solution. We are living in a constant fear of family separation because he's the

64
00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:49.440
only one we have. We cannot send him back, as there is no one there who can

65
00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:54.315
properly care of him. We have worked hard since our college years to build a life

66
00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.895
in New Zealand and contribute to this beautiful country.

67
00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:02.805
Then we have started a petition to seek support and are continuing our effort to

68
00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:03.900
fight for our son.

69
00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:08.940
Aiden is a joyful and deeply loved child who has a strong interest in music,

70
00:05:09.031 --> 00:05:12.404
swinging, and all the outdoor activities.

71
00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:18.330
He's generally a calm boy, but unfortunately, he's diagnosed with autism spectrum

72
00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:23.910
disorder. And the decision to deport and reject his visa is deeply

73
00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:29.940
distressing and feel unjust. It's profoundly concerning that in this day and age, a

74
00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:33.420
child is not being fully considered due to his disability.

75
00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:37.470
Such action can seem a lack of compassion and do not reflect the value of an

76
00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:40.800
inclusive and human society.

77
00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.980
Our son, Aiden, has potential to achieve many things if he get the support from his

78
00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:51.570
parents and the society. So this all about my story.

79
00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:53.265
Thank you so much.

80
00:05:53.281 --> 00:05:55.140
Well, thank you.

81
00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:58.440
Yeah. And over to you now, Frans.

82
00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:03.031
Hey, good day, everyone. Thanks for the time.

83
00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:05.940
Yeah, Chair, members of the committee,

84
00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:10.560
yeah, thank you for the few minutes that we can share our story here.

85
00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:16.065
My name is Frans Merrits, and I'm here for my son, my family, and every migrant

86
00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:18.781
family affected by the acceptable standard of health.

87
00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:21.570
Our story is quite personal.

88
00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:27.690
And sorry if my voice is going to get croaky because it's been a very long battle.

89
00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:30.570
But this problem is much bigger than just us.

90
00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:32.820
So for almost 10 years,

91
00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:38.670
the immigration system kept our son away from our family because he did not meet

92
00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:44.610
the ASSH policy. My son suffered a stroke at birth, which was nothing

93
00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:49.410
to do, you know, his fault. He has a speech and development delay,

94
00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:53.189
but has improved significantly as a human being.

95
00:06:54.689 --> 00:07:00.390
But that doesn't define him. He is my son, he is a brother to my boys, and he's a

96
00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:01.020
human being.

97
00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:07.290
And we lost almost 10 years together because a policy calculated what he might cost

98
00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:07.980
New Zealand.

99
00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:14.970
10 years. That's 10 birthdays, 10 Christmases, brothers growing apart, moments

100
00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:15.901
we'll never get back.

101
00:07:17.341 --> 00:07:22.500
So I ask you, with tears in my eyes, you know, what's 10 years worth of a child's

102
00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:22.860
life?

103
00:07:24.901 --> 00:07:30.360
ASSH calculates the potential cost of my son, but who calculates the cost of ASSH

104
00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:31.216
on our family?

105
00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:36.841
We are paying it now. We're picking up pieces of a family damaged by years of

106
00:07:36.901 --> 00:07:37.620
separation.

107
00:07:39.225 --> 00:07:42.061
And we will have to carry that life sentence for a very long time.

108
00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:49.305
Throughout this journey, particularly on social media, we have heard, you know, "If

109
00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:51.660
you don't like it here, go back to your own country."

110
00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:53.280
Mm.

111
00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:57.091
But the Kiwi who actually knows us have said something very different.

112
00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:02.430
They said, "Frans, this is wrong. I am ashamed this is happening in New Zealand."

113
00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.160
Surely that tells us something.

114
00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:11.730
When ordinary New Zealanders look at policy and say, "This is not how Kiwis

115
00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:15.180
represent the world", shouldn't we listen?

116
00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:21.030
And to those who tell us to go back, I'm saying a hard no.

117
00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:22.980
This is my country as well.

118
00:08:23.835 --> 00:08:23.835
Mm.

119
00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:27.510
We stayed because we love New Zealand. We fought because we believe in it.

120
00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:33.990
And even while our family was hurting, we kept giving back to our community.

121
00:08:34.170 --> 00:08:36.211
I personally have built businesses here,

122
00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.390
and I've coached junior rugby for years.

123
00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:42.091
Here in my local area in Beachlands,

124
00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:46.651
I volunteered as a club president. I've fundraised a lot.

125
00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:47.056
Mm.

126
00:08:47.550 --> 00:08:49.440
And I'm doing it because I love the sport.

127
00:08:49.561 --> 00:08:55.530
I love to see how the sport changes young men or young boys into incredible

128
00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:55.890
men.

129
00:08:57.390 --> 00:09:00.780
And coaching isn't just about rugby, it's about the discipline, the respect, the

130
00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:01.500
resilience,

131
00:09:03.090 --> 00:09:05.370
and about helping boys become, like I said, better men

132
00:09:07.795 --> 00:09:09.504
So what is that contribution worth?

133
00:09:10.944 --> 00:09:13.224
What if I had arrived here with a heart condition?

134
00:09:13.554 --> 00:09:13.659
Would

135
00:09:15.354 --> 00:09:16.854
that have made me worth less?

136
00:09:18.534 --> 00:09:23.994
Could a medical assessment have predicted my contribution to my community? No.

137
00:09:25.464 --> 00:09:28.944
And if you couldn't calculate my potential, how can you calculate my son's

138
00:09:28.974 --> 00:09:33.834
potential? Human potential cannot be measured on a spreadsheet.

139
00:09:35.874 --> 00:09:39.684
I understand our health system and education systems are under pressure,

140
00:09:41.334 --> 00:09:44.514
but has ESS become the easy answer to a difficult problem?

141
00:09:45.534 --> 00:09:50.664
If healthcare is struggling, we need to fix it, and if education is struggling with

142
00:09:50.724 --> 00:09:52.463
resources, we need to fix that too.

143
00:09:54.894 --> 00:09:57.744
Do not make children pay for problems they did not create.

144
00:09:59.364 --> 00:10:03.984
New Zealand has committed itself to the right and dignity of disabled people, yet

145
00:10:04.014 --> 00:10:08.859
the United Nations has already raised concerns about discrimination resulting from

146
00:10:08.904 --> 00:10:14.679
this ESS policy. What are those commitments worth if we hide behind policy when

147
00:10:14.754 --> 00:10:17.004
these become difficult or expensive?

148
00:10:18.864 --> 00:10:23.589
Our family has already paid the price. You cannot give us those 10 years back.

149
00:10:24.714 --> 00:10:27.354
But you can stop another family from losing theirs.

150
00:10:28.614 --> 00:10:32.484
I am not here for sympathy. I'm not asking for special treatment.

151
00:10:33.295 --> 00:10:37.344
I'm asking for change. Our experience cannot be undone.

152
00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:45.264
But let it mean something. Let it become the reason another child doesn't lose 10

153
00:10:45.325 --> 00:10:46.254
years with their family.

154
00:10:48.654 --> 00:10:52.869
We love New Zealand dearly. We love it enough to believe we can do better.

155
00:10:55.254 --> 00:10:58.644
And you are the lawmakers. You have the power to change this.

156
00:11:00.174 --> 00:11:03.264
ESS is unjust, it's outdated, and it's broken.

157
00:11:06.174 --> 00:11:09.774
I'm not asking for it to be adjusted.

158
00:11:11.244 --> 00:11:16.644
I'm not to be moving the threshold. But we're asking you to abolish it completely.

159
00:11:17.814 --> 00:11:20.814
And let's build a better New Zealand together the way it should be.

160
00:11:22.404 --> 00:11:22.884
Thank you.

161
00:11:25.404 --> 00:11:30.594
All right. Thank you, all of you. It's very emotional and very difficult, so I

162
00:11:30.624 --> 00:11:35.694
appreciate your contribution here today.

163
00:11:35.784 --> 00:11:38.094
Now, the committee have some questions. Greg Fleming.

164
00:11:38.904 --> 00:11:43.674
Yeah. Hey, thank you guys very much for sharing the stories as vulnerably as you

165
00:11:43.705 --> 00:11:49.450
did. Just want to clarify, so you're asking for there to be no standard of

166
00:11:49.464 --> 00:11:52.944
health applied. Is that right?

167
00:11:53.124 --> 00:11:55.854
Anya speaking. Yeah, that is what we're asking.

168
00:11:56.739 --> 00:12:02.154
And the reason for that is that the logic that says that

169
00:12:02.184 --> 00:12:07.884
disabled people, people with health conditions are a cost burden, that's a

170
00:12:07.914 --> 00:12:13.614
harmful logic to apply to anyone. So whether that's to

171
00:12:14.034 --> 00:12:19.134
a child, disabled child, as you've heard, or an adult with a disability or a health

172
00:12:19.194 --> 00:12:23.545
condition or high BMI gets caught in this policy as well.

173
00:12:24.354 --> 00:12:28.884
So we say that we want to start from a strength-based position, a position that

174
00:12:29.004 --> 00:12:33.594
values human beings and their potential and their contributions that they will

175
00:12:33.624 --> 00:12:38.545
bring, and that they will also bring better as family units when you keep a family

176
00:12:38.604 --> 00:12:44.288
together and put in place the conditions where they can all thrive and

177
00:12:44.514 --> 00:12:47.244
give back to their fullest potential.

178
00:12:47.304 --> 00:12:51.038
Yeah, no, I appreciate that. Do you think that genuinely it is an anthropological

179
00:12:51.054 --> 00:12:57.024
question, though? Do you think it's one of the policy is just a result of us

180
00:12:57.144 --> 00:12:59.545
living, unfortunately, in a resource-constrained world?

181
00:13:01.314 --> 00:13:02.244
So the policy

182
00:13:03.654 --> 00:13:09.564
is a political choice. In Canada, the similar policy, their medical

183
00:13:09.714 --> 00:13:13.554
inadmissibility was reviewed back in 2017.

184
00:13:13.614 --> 00:13:16.674
There's a reference for that in the written submission.

185
00:13:17.364 --> 00:13:23.124
And it was lessened considerably, with a path to potentially

186
00:13:23.154 --> 00:13:28.284
removing it entirely over time. And that was specifically on

187
00:13:28.884 --> 00:13:34.674
noting that the values that underpin that policy didn't align with kind of

188
00:13:34.704 --> 00:13:38.499
modern Canadian values of compassion and inclusiveness and things like that.

189
00:13:38.545 --> 00:13:43.434
So, with the political will, this policy can be changed.

190
00:13:44.154 --> 00:13:49.779
Yes, we need to resource health and education systems better, but there are other

191
00:13:49.795 --> 00:13:54.174
ways to raise revenue to do that that don't essentially involve scapegoating our

192
00:13:54.204 --> 00:13:55.585
migrants.

193
00:13:55.644 --> 00:13:56.708
Okay. Thank you.

194
00:13:56.784 --> 00:13:57.954
Oh, Sulia White-Brown.

195
00:13:58.374 --> 00:14:03.864
Thank you. Anya and colleagues, you brought some very moving stories to us.

196
00:14:04.254 --> 00:14:09.503
And in fact, you started, Anya, on what I want to know more about, which is the

197
00:14:09.534 --> 00:14:15.504
Canadian system. And have you-- And if you haven't, don't worry, we

198
00:14:15.564 --> 00:14:21.204
can ask for information. Have you heard about any positive or negative

199
00:14:21.265 --> 00:14:24.204
results after they lowered the bar?

200
00:14:24.445 --> 00:14:28.464
I mean, the bar at the moment seems to me to be a breach of human rights, but we

201
00:14:28.494 --> 00:14:31.825
have some problems with challenging that at the moment.

202
00:14:33.654 --> 00:14:38.259
Well, there's one family who tried for years and years to be able to get their

203
00:14:38.304 --> 00:14:43.884
autistic daughter over here. And then the father, who'd been living here

204
00:14:44.244 --> 00:14:47.214
because they were a split family, ended up getting a job in Canada.

205
00:14:47.424 --> 00:14:51.984
And because they'd removed the education criteria from Canada's, they went to

206
00:14:52.045 --> 00:14:54.744
Canada, and they had no problem, and they got in.

207
00:14:54.774 --> 00:14:58.795
And my heart just kind of broke for them. But there are examples like that.

208
00:15:00.144 --> 00:15:05.244
And so, yeah, many of the families impacted at the moment, it is under

209
00:15:05.394 --> 00:15:07.795
education criteria.

210
00:15:09.354 --> 00:15:12.594
I think it could be worthwhile talking to Canadian officials.

211
00:15:12.654 --> 00:15:14.604
I'm sure you guys have the means to do that.

212
00:15:14.649 --> 00:15:18.774
And yeah, there are a couple of sources there in the written submission as well.

213
00:15:20.034 --> 00:15:20.424
Thank you.

214
00:15:20.754 --> 00:15:23.545
All right. Thanks. Any other questions, members?

215
00:15:23.754 --> 00:15:25.374
Oh, sorry, can I ask one clarifying question?

216
00:15:25.434 --> 00:15:26.019
So Frans-

217
00:15:26.094 --> 00:15:26.754
That's Greg Fleming.

218
00:15:26.934 --> 00:15:31.494
Yeah, sorry. So Frans, where has your son been for these last 10 years?

219
00:15:35.634 --> 00:15:39.445
Sorry, I'm spying on my new button. He's with my parents in South Africa.

220
00:15:41.364 --> 00:15:46.015
So yeah, I don't want to make a long thing about it, but yeah, it's a decision we

221
00:15:46.104 --> 00:15:49.524
made to come over here. We thought it was going to be a quick thing.

222
00:15:49.795 --> 00:15:51.924
We've been fighting the battle ever since.

223
00:15:51.954 --> 00:15:53.784
But we've committed ourselves to New Zealand.

224
00:15:54.114 --> 00:15:59.304
We've been in so deep that there's no-- For us to turn around now and go back would

225
00:15:59.394 --> 00:16:03.354
be everything would be a waste. We'll rather just keep fighting.

226
00:16:04.254 --> 00:16:09.789
I still have hope for New Zealand, and who knows, maybe this was my destiny for my

227
00:16:09.835 --> 00:16:13.045
life to come to New Zealand and do this. I don't know.

228
00:16:14.335 --> 00:16:14.379
But I try and-

229
00:16:14.394 --> 00:16:19.734
So just so I'm clear, you made the decision, though, to move to South Africa

230
00:16:19.765 --> 00:16:23.244
knowing that there was a chance that your son wouldn't be able to come?

231
00:16:23.814 --> 00:16:24.114
Well-

232
00:16:24.894 --> 00:16:25.374
New Zealand.

233
00:16:25.614 --> 00:16:26.214
Yeah.

234
00:16:27.744 --> 00:16:32.304
So we came over, we applied. All our family's got given visas.

235
00:16:32.844 --> 00:16:35.064
