290
00:19:34.644 --> 00:19:38.754
Fundamentally, the Immigration Act requires the immigration system to balance the

291
00:19:38.784 --> 00:19:41.140
national interest with individual rights.

292
00:19:41.754 --> 00:19:46.539
It must facilitate migration while reducing risks to public health and minimizing

293
00:19:46.644 --> 00:19:50.725
significant cost and demand on New Zealand's health and living support services.

294
00:19:51.624 --> 00:19:55.464
With the medical waiver provisions providing the flexibility to consider individual

295
00:19:55.494 --> 00:19:57.324
circumstances where appropriate.

296
00:19:58.464 --> 00:20:02.334
These acceptable standard of health settings have operated for more than 20 years

297
00:20:02.424 --> 00:20:07.074
under successive governments and provide a consistent way to assess health-related

298
00:20:07.104 --> 00:20:12.444
