00:30:12.102 --> 00:30:16.242
What if parents had not had the knowledge that my mom had?

481
00:30:16.302 --> 00:30:20.622
What if they simply thought I was struggling with reading and writing, and I would

482
00:30:20.652 --> 00:30:21.658
eventually catch up?

483
00:30:23.172 --> 00:30:27.313
I think about the families across New Zealand who are in this exact same position

484
00:30:27.763 --> 00:30:29.772
because not every parent is a teacher.

485
00:30:30.643 --> 00:30:36.552
Not every parent knows that their child may be different, and they

486
00:30:36.643 --> 00:30:40.152
may need special conditions and special learning things.

487
00:30:40.302 --> 00:30:43.917
This means that there could be many students across Aotearoa who are slipping

488
00:30:43.932 --> 00:30:48.956
through the cracks at this very moment because no one around them recognize what is

489
00:30:48.972 --> 00:30:52.513
happening and what their brain is thinking.

490
00:30:52.542 --> 00:30:56.682
And this is why early identification of dyslexia matters so much.

491
00:30:57.057 --> 00:31:00.703
Because dyslexia does not determine how intelligent I am.

492
00:31:00.792 --> 00:31:04.242
It does not determine how hard I work.

493
00:31:04.302 --> 00:31:06.582
But it does determine how much

494
00:31:08.232 --> 00:31:11.112
I struggle in school, and how much school becomes a burden for me.

495
00:31:12.192 --> 00:31:15.402
For me, this petition is fundamentally about fairness.

496
00:31:16.302 --> 00:31:17.953
It is whether or not

497
00:31:19.422 --> 00:31:23.247
access to understanding of how you learn should depend on your parents' income,

498
00:31:23.563 --> 00:31:27.822
where you live, or whether your parents can afford hundreds or even thousands of

499
00:31:27.882 --> 00:31:31.362
dollars for a dyslexia diagnostic assessment.

500
00:31:31.376 --> 00:31:35.067
The Ministry of Education has told this committee that dyslexia assessments in New

501
00:31:35.143 --> 00:31:40.122
Zealand are not typically publicly funded, and families often have to pay

502
00:31:40.152 --> 00:31:45.522
privately. Their own submission states that assessments commonly cost between $700

503
00:31:45.536 --> 00:31:50.487
and $1,500. For most families in New Zealand, this may be manageable, but for a lot

504
00:31:50.533 --> 00:31:55.272
of families, this is an enormous amount of money, and it will really have a

505
00:31:55.453 --> 00:31:58.257
negative effect, and will mean that they actually can't access this.

506
00:31:58.768 --> 00:32:02.893
This creates a problem of equity. If two students with the same learning

507
00:32:02.953 --> 00:32:07.932
difficulties like dyslexia and dyslexia, but one of the students can afford an

508
00:32:07.992 --> 00:32:11.547
assessment and the others can't, we should ask ourselves whether or not we are

509
00:32:11.592 --> 00:32:14.652
comfortable with that difference and opportunities that can follow.

510
00:32:14.697 --> 00:32:18.852
And I would encourage, and I would think that everyone on this committee would

511
00:32:18.972 --> 00:32:24.866
agree otherwise. The Ministry has also made the point that it is,

512
00:32:25.152 --> 00:32:30.912
in its response, it says that students do not need a formal diagnosis to receive

513
00:32:30.942 --> 00:32:35.292
learning support, and that this should be consistent across all schools in New

514
00:32:35.352 --> 00:32:39.507
Zealand. Support should be based on individual learning needs.

515
00:32:39.522 --> 00:32:43.272
But I can tell you from firsthand experience that this is not the case.

516
00:32:43.662 --> 00:32:48.013
Because I have a dyslexia diagnosis, and I sent that to my school, and they came

517
00:32:48.042 --> 00:32:51.972
back and said it is either out of date, and I did it four years ago.

518
00:32:53.082 --> 00:32:57.252
And for me, and for everyone, dyslexia does not disappear in four years.

519
00:32:57.462 --> 00:33:01.063
It is a lifelong specialty that we have.

520
00:33:01.497 --> 00:33:07.302
And I was only given a computer for my exams rather than a reader-writer or using

521
00:33:07.513 --> 00:33:10.902
Dictate, and rather than handwriting my exams.

522
00:33:11.232 --> 00:33:14.742
And for me, there's no difference between typing on a computer and handwriting the

523
00:33:14.772 --> 00:33:19.482
exams. The problem is, is that the thoughts up here, I cannot translate to paper

524
00:33:19.513 --> 00:33:23.772
because of spelling, reading, and just general difficulties around that.

525
00:33:24.763 --> 00:33:26.682
And because there is a difference between,

526
00:33:28.302 --> 00:33:31.422
if the government recognizes that diagnosis can

527
00:33:31.722 --> 00:33:37.482
access and help people have support easier, then

528
00:33:37.572 --> 00:33:43.513
we must ask ourselves, why isn't diagnosis accessible for all families, depending

529
00:33:43.692 --> 00:33:48.401
even though we may have whanau that can't afford it or who are living in poverty.

530
00:33:48.672 --> 00:33:52.572
This is simply not right. The Ministry also points out that work is being

531
00:33:52.632 --> 00:33:55.242
undertaken for identifying dyslexia.

532
00:33:55.302 --> 00:33:59.143
It refers to structured literacy, phonics checks, teacher training, and learning

533
00:33:59.232 --> 00:34:03.072
support coordinators, and other interventions that are designed to identify

534
00:34:03.102 --> 00:34:08.893
students with dyslexia. I support these interventions, but screening in the

535
00:34:08.953 --> 00:34:12.432
classroom and receiving comprehensive diagnosis are not the same.

536
00:34:12.852 --> 00:34:16.752
Teachers can identify when students are struggling. Schools can provide support.

537
00:34:16.812 --> 00:34:17.533
But a proper

538
00:34:20.203 --> 00:34:23.998
qualified specialist can provide a formal assessment that gives students and their

539
00:34:24.072 --> 00:34:27.522
whanau a clear understanding on their learning needs when it comes to dyslexia.

540
00:34:28.002 --> 00:34:33.822
I think we should have both, because early identification is especially important.

541
00:34:33.882 --> 00:34:38.292
Because the Ministry's own submission referred to the 2016 select committee inquiry

542
00:34:38.352 --> 00:34:42.672
that recommended strengthening our identification practices and achieving greater

543
00:34:42.703 --> 00:34:44.802
consistency and support across New Zealand.

544
00:34:45.042 --> 00:34:49.662
10 years later, we are still discussing this problem today, and many rangatahi

545
00:34:49.692 --> 00:34:54.672
across this country are still experiencing not consistent support.

546
00:34:55.272 --> 00:34:57.912
So that should tell us that there's more work to be done.

547
00:34:58.287 --> 00:35:01.092
That brings me to the moral argument behind my petition.

548
00:35:01.812 --> 00:35:05.112
We need to ask ourselves, what kind of education system do we want to have?

549
00:35:05.472 --> 00:35:09.732
Do we want a system where opportunity to understand our own learning depends on our

550
00:35:09.792 --> 00:35:13.887
family's financial position, or do we want a system where every person has a fair

551
00:35:13.932 --> 00:35:16.257
opportunity to understand their learning needs?

552
00:35:17.052 --> 00:35:19.587
For me, this is a question about basic fairness.

553
00:35:20.112 --> 00:35:20.322
If we

554
00:35:21.882 --> 00:35:25.857
believe our education system is a public good, which it is in New Zealand, then

555
00:35:25.873 --> 00:35:30.297
identifying barriers to education should be treated as a public responsibility,

556
00:35:30.342 --> 00:35:33.462
because a child does not choose if they have dyslexia.

557
00:35:33.522 --> 00:35:37.542
A family does not choose to struggle financially, and a student should not have to

558
00:35:37.572 --> 00:35:41.712
choose between paying for an assessment and whanau putting food on the table.

559
00:35:41.998 --> 00:35:46.722
That is wrong. That is why I'm not asking the government to simply spend money

560
00:35:46.782 --> 00:35:51.072
without consideration. I'm asking the government to consider the long-term cost of

561
00:35:51.132 --> 00:35:54.522
not early identification for our rangatahi in our schools.

562
00:35:54.762 --> 00:35:55.992
Because when dyslexia-

